   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/7283266ebb96abf5.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by Chih-chun Janet Lin/ResearchGate)</figcaption>\n</figure>",
   "stem_html": "<p>The phylogenetic tree compares the DNA of some bacteria with the DNA found in mitochondria and chloroplasts.</p>\n<p>Based on this information, make a hypothesis about how early eukaryote cells obtained chloroplasts and mitochondria.&lt;,/p&gt;</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1246962,
     "content_html": "Early eukaryotes cells evolved mitochondria and got chloroplasts through endosymbiosis."
    },
    {
     "id": 1246961,
     "content_html": "Early eukaryotes cells evolved chloroplasts and got mitochondria through endosymbiosis."
    },
    {
     "id": 1246963,
     "content_html": "Early eukaryotes cells obtained mitochondria and chloroplasts from two separate endoysmbiosis events."
    },
    {
     "id": 1246960,
     "content_html": "Early eukaryotes cells obtained mitochondria and chloroplasts from a single endosymbiosis event."
    }
